'''''Veronica longifolia''''', known as '''garden speedwell'''<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |access-date=2014-10-17 }}</ref> or '''longleaf speedwell''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=PSLO6|taxon=Pseudolysimachion longifolium|access-date=15 October 2015}}</ref> is a [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Plantaginaceae]] where many introduced varieties in North America are native to Europe and Western Asia.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Veronica longifolia (Longleaf Speedwell) |url=https://www.gardenia.net/genus/veronica-longifolia-speedwell |access-date=2026-06-01 |website=Gardenia |language=en-US}}</ref>

==Description==
[[File:Veronica longifolia Przetacznik długolistny 2020-07-12 02.jpg|thumb|Full view of plant in bloom.]]
[[File:Veronica longifolia Przetacznik długolistny 2020-07-12 06.jpg|thumb|Seed pods after flowering period.]]
This [[herbaceous]] [[perennial plant|perennial]] is {{convert|2|-|4|ft|cm|-1|order=flip|abbr=on}} tall and spreads to {{convert|2|ft|cm|-1|order=flip|abbr=on}}. The flower spikes are {{convert|10|-|12|in|cm|0|order=flip|abbr=on}} long and bear lilac to purple blooms.<ref>{{cite book|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=557KJL0TC48C&q=Veronica+longifolia&pg=PA408|editor=Frances Tenenbaum|title=Taylor's Encyclopedia of Garden Plants|series=Taylor's Guides|year=2003|page=408|isbn=0-61822644-3}}</ref> The foliage is lance-shaped with dark green leaves that are arranged oppositely along the stem.<ref name=":0" />

